1a07d7a016e159a10d892e81b0"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G1G2","usage":{"input_tokens":96704,"output_tokens":2786,"requests":5}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"3c0ed0f5d58b454c1a9a78ad613344e7615a2868674b99f85ae974e03314cef1"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":121264,"output_tokens":5032,"requests":7}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py:442 to the conversion scope (its `_run([\"rebar\", ...])` wraps subprocess.run), and extend the step-2 detector to resolve argv passed through local subprocess-wrapper helpers like `_run`, so helper-routed bare-`rebar` launches are both converted and guarded.","cohort":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3844,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'A syntax-tree scan of tests/ found the same PATH dependence at 38 sites in 22 modules besides this one' and '35 real child-process calls ... whose argv begins with the literal \"rebar\"'","Plan step 2: fails on 'any call to a subprocess-launching function whose first argv element is the literal \"rebar\"'","tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py:442: `result = _run([\"rebar\", \"verify-identity\"], cwd=client, env=env, check=False)`","tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py:36-37: `_run` wraps `subprocess.run(argv, cwd=cwd, env=env, ...)` — argv[0]=='rebar' reaches a real subprocess launcher","This file is absent from the plan's 22-module list and is not the test_changed_criteria module"],"finding":"The scope inventory ('38 sites in 22 modules') and the step-2 policy detector both key on a direct subprocess-launcher call whose argv[0] is the literal \"rebar\", and so omit tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py:442, which launches the CLI via a helper. That line calls `_run([\"rebar\", \"verify-identity\"], cwd=client, env=env, check=False)`, and `_run` (defined at lines 29-45 of the same file) wraps `subprocess.run(argv, ...)` — a genuine PATH-dependent bare-`rebar` child process that is neither in the 22-module list nor catchable by the proposed syntax-tree check (its callee is the local `_run`, not a subprocess launcher).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc960a49b636d5c80","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context 'Scope: the whole class' — 'A syntax-tree scan of tests/ found the same PATH dependence at 38 sites in 22 modules besides this one'; Plan step 2 detector","norm_id":"n0a2d6628ae74d1da","priority":0.5156,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py:442 keeps launching PATH's rebar after the change — the exact PATH-dependence the ticket set out to eliminate remains in this integration test, and breaks the same way once the global copy's `verify-identity` behaviour drifts.","The new test_no_bare_rebar_subprocess.py, keyed on direct launcher calls, does not flag helper-wrapped argv like `_run([\"rebar\", ...])`, so the regression guard reports green while a live bare-`rebar` launch survives."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Convert line 442 to `_run([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"rebar\", \"verify-identity\"], ...)`, and have the policy check treat first-argv `\"rebar\"` passed to known local subprocess wrappers (helpers that themselves call subprocess.run/Popen on their argv parameter) as a violation, not only direct subprocess launcher calls.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"insufficient","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"insufficient","impa